system "ISO:ben-Beng:Latn:15919-2026" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 15919-2026
  language iso-639-2:ben
  source_script Beng
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO/DIS 15919 (2026) Information and documentation -- Transliteration of Indic scripts into Latin characters (Bengali (and Assamese); DIS stage)"
  url https://www.iso.org/committee/48820.html
  creation_date 2026
  adoption_date 2026
  description {    Second edition (DIS stage) of ISO 15919, Transliteration of Indic scripts into Latin characters.
    Encoded from the committee ballot ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N125; per-script tables of clause 7,
    numerals of normative Annex A, Rule 17 Vedic accents, and options 9.8/9.9/9.10 as
    selectable variants (languages opt98 opt99 opt10). See notes for provenance and errata.  }

  notes {
    note "Encoded from ISO/DIS 15919 (2026), ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N125 (DIS stage draft, 2026-01-26), Table 7.2 plus the numerals of normative Annex A Table A.2; shared-table content verified against ISO/CD 15919 (2025, N108) and ISO 15919 WD (2024, N88). The DIS is not yet a published International Standard."
    note "Rule 2 convention: inherent a with a consonant is always transliterated (consonant rows carry the inherent a)."
    note "virama is deleted in the default behavior (clause 6 printed virama hex list); option 9.10 (language selector opt10) instead renders virama as middle dot U+00B7."
    note "Option selectors (W3 languages, single-select): opt98 = clause 9.8 upper-case for all initial vowels (first letter capitalised for digraph outputs); opt99 = clause 9.9 unusual conjuncts marked with equals sign U+003D via the script's zero-width joiner; opt10 = clause 9.10 explicit virama middle dot. Option 9.1 (non-uniform e/o) is available by character substitution on outputs and is not separately staged."
    note "DIS erratum recorded: Table 7.2 row ba+nukta (09AC 09BC) prints Latin 'wa' with Hex 0066 (contradiction); the Latin text 'wa' is encoded."
    note "Cross-check (audit axis): Wikipedia ISO 15919 table (2001-reflected) vs corpus map agreement 44/66 printed rows; systematic divergences recorded as findings, not fixes: vocalic r/l rows (corpus ṛ-family vs ISO r̥-family), long e/o rows (corpus e/o vs ISO ē/ō), avagraha (corpus :’ vs ISO ')."
    note "Row-level source errata encoded per printed text: Table 7.2 row ['ব়']: latin/hex mismatch: text='wa' hex=0066"
    note "The precomposed nukta letters 09DC 09DD 09DF are encoded alongside their decomposed combinations (clause 7.3: precomposed and decomposed characters are treated equally on input)."
  }
}

languages opt98 opt99 opt10

tests {
   "অ" ->  "a"
   "ক" ->  "ka"
   "আ" ->  "ā"
   "া" ->  "ā"
   "খ" ->  "kha"
   "ই" ->  "i"
   "ি" ->  "i"
   "গ" ->  "ga"
   "ঈ" ->  "ī"
   "ী" ->  "ī"
   "ঘ" ->  "gha"
